## Footer inventory (`PUBLIC_FOOTER_LINKS`)

Sitewide footer columns in `web/src/lib/config/constants/config.ts` — keep aligned when adding hubs or tools:

| Column | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| **Tools** | `/tools`, `/tools/skill-builder`, `/tools/photo-editor`, `/tools/humanizer`, `/tools/best-time-to-post` |
| **Directories** | `/playbooks`, `/building-blocks`, `/creators`, category/tag index paths |
| **Resources** | `/agents`, `/channels`, `/alternatives`, `/blog`, `/compare`, `/docs`, self-host install |
| **Company** | `/about`, `/roadmap`, `/pricing`, Discord |

New pSEO routes that should be discoverable from every page belong here or in header nav config — not only in FAQ cross-links.

## PR checklist (pSEO FAQ + copy)

- [ ] FAQ answers follow ASD-STE100 (short, active, one idea per sentence).
- [ ] Connect questions: sign-up and/or connect guide before operator docs.
- [ ] Any `/docs/social-integration/` link uses `faqLinkSelfHostChannelSetup` or anchor text containing `self-host`.
- [ ] `publicFaqLinks.test.ts` + channel-level tests: `href="/sign-up"` or connect guide on connect FAQs; no unlabeled social-integration anchors.
- [ ] Hub FAQ wired: constants → `createPublicFaqSEOSchema` in `+page.server.ts` → `PublicFaq` in `+page.svelte` → forward in `+page.ts`.
- [ ] JSON-LD `Answer.text` matches visible accordion (no raw `<a>` tags).
- [ ] Meta + canonical + JSON-LD `url` use the same `buildCanonicalUrl` (**web-seo-canonical**).

